# Dev-only sub-path reverse-proxy test (ROADMAP P0 item 4: "SWOC2_BASE_PATH and the forwarded
# headers work, tested behind Caddy, also on a sub-path. HTTP mode works without certificates.")
# Deliberately plain HTTP, no TLS - the publicly-trusted-certificate reverse proxy for
# locked-down service computers (GEN-014, ADR 0014) is a separate, P3 concern.
#
# Run the app itself with SWOC2_BASE_PATH=/swoc2/ wherever it's reachable on the host
# (docs/TESTING.md §3.3), then this strips the /swoc2 prefix before forwarding and tells the
# app it did, via X-Forwarded-Prefix, so Spring's ForwardedHeaderFilter (toggled by
# SWOC2_FORWARDED_HEADERS) regenerates redirects - notably the OAuth2 login callback - with the
# prefix put back on.
:6443 {
	handle_path /swoc2/* {
		reverse_proxy host.docker.internal:5080 {
			header_up X-Forwarded-Prefix /swoc2
		}
	}
}
